          "distinct": true,
          "id": "dc9a67705fa2175078507365eec339fddc135863",
          "message": "fix(dispatch-plan): mirror registry plan_package semantics (#3691) (#3724)\n\nMulti-area issues planned as first-of-sorted area while the registry\ncross-check computes the GLOBAL serializing partition — the disagreement\nperma-deferred every multi-area ready issue at dispatch (live: #3390,\n#3391 head-of-line blocking the whole frontier). Exactly one unique\narea maps to that area; zero or multiple map to __global__, mirroring\nregistry plan_package byte-for-byte. Three fixtures + a mutation\ntripwire (old pick goes red).\n\nCo-authored-by: sparq-agent <sparq-agent@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-22T05:30:42Z",
